# Gate-defining files: changes here can create, weaken, or bypass a quality
# gate -- the coverage floor, lint rules, complexity limit, strict
# type-checking, the secret scanner, the dead-code allowlist, the CI
# workflows that run all of it, the dependency lockfile a CVE scan reads, or
# the scripts that ratchet/report on all of the above. They must not change
# without a human reviewing the diff -- an autonomous agent editing one of
# these lines should not be able to merge on its own say-so.
#
# Enforcement: this file only takes effect once branch protection on the
# default branch has "Require review from Code Owners" enabled (a repo
# setting outside this file, the user's to turn on) -- and only once this
# file itself is merged to the default branch, so it does not retroactively
# gate the PR that first introduces it. See docs/agent-safety.md.

/pyproject.toml               @hungranger
/.pre-commit-config.yaml      @hungranger
/.github/                     @hungranger
/.gitleaks.toml                @hungranger
/.vulture_allowlist.py        @hungranger
/uv.lock                      @hungranger
/scripts/gate_ratchet.py      @hungranger
/scripts/suppression_diff.py  @hungranger
/scripts/mutation_score.py    @hungranger
